It is late on Thursday evening.
I am finally back in the flat and relaxing.
I take the mobile phone and start a video call.
I call my family in Mexico.
My mother answers immediately.
"Hello Maya!"
"How was your day?" she asks.
"Very good," I answer.
"I played badminton today."
"And I talked a lot with Timo and Lena."
"What did you tell them?" my mother asks.
"I told them the whole story," I say.
"I mentioned the papers and the job."
"And I talked a lot about my first week in January."
My mother smiles and looks into the camera.
"You have really experienced a lot," she says softly.
"Did you also tell them about our goodbye at the airport?"
I shake my head.
"No, I haven't told that to anyone yet," I say.
She nods slowly.
"I also thought about that morning today," she says.
